  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>resize</keyword>
  <short_description>Resize an array by truncating or padding.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>B = resize(A, m)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>B = resize(A, sz)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>B = resize(A, sz, 'FillValue', v)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>A</param_name>
      <param_description>the array to resize.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>m</param_name>
      <param_description>a scalar length, used to resize a vector.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>sz</param_name>
      <param_description>a size vector <b>[m n ...]</b> giving the size of the result.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>v</param_name>
      <param_description>the value used to fill added elements (default <b>0</b> for a numeric array).</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>B</param_name>
      <param_description>the resized array, of the requested size and the class of <b>A</b>.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>resize</b> returns an array of the requested size. Along each
      dimension, elements of <b>A</b> beyond the new size are dropped and
      positions beyond the original data are filled with a fill value, which is
      <b>0</b> for a numeric array unless <b>'FillValue'</b> is given. A scalar
      size resizes the length of a vector and keeps its orientation.</p>
  </description>
